  c) offer the Software, or its functions, to others as a hosted, online or managed service;
  d) modify, translate, adapt or create derivative works of the Software;
  e) decompile, disassemble or reverse engineer the Software, or try to derive its source
     code, algorithms or methods;
  f) copy or reuse any of the Software's code in another product;
  g) remove, change or hide any copyright, trademark or other notice in the Software;
  h) get around any license key, activation, payment or usage limit the Software has now
     or may have in a future version; or
  i) use the Software in a way section 6 does not allow.

Some of the Software is installed as human-readable script files (for example, .py files).
They are provided only so that the Software can run on your computer. Being able to read
