5. Your content and your responsibilities

Videos, scripts, captions, clips and other material you put into or create with the
Software ("Your Content") belong to you or to their owners. Licensor claims no ownership
of Your Content.

You are solely responsible for Your Content and for how you use the Software. In
particular, you are responsible for:

  a) having the rights or permissions needed for any video you download, process, clip,
     edit or publish with the Software;
  b) complying with the terms of service of any website or platform you download from or
     publish to (such as YouTube, Google Drive, TikTok, Instagram or X), and with the rules
     of any clipping marketplace or program you take part in; and
  c) the accounts and sign-ins you use with the Software, and any cookies file you create
     for it.

The Software's ability to download or process a video does not mean you are allowed to
use that video.


6. Acceptable use

You may not use the Software, or any voice, picture, text or video it produces, to:

  a) break any law, or infringe anyone's copyright, trademark, privacy, publicity or other
     rights;
  b) impersonate a real person, or make content that falsely presents a real person as
     saying or doing something (a "deepfake"), without that person's consent;
  c) deceive people, including by presenting AI-generated content as real where that is
     misleading or where the law or a platform's rules require it to be labelled;
  d) harass, threaten, defame or exploit anyone, or make sexual content involving minors;
  e) spread illegal content, malware, spam or fraud; or
  f) do anything the license of an included AI model forbids (see section 7).


7. Third-party components and AI models

The Software includes or downloads third-party components, such as Electron, Python
libraries, FFmpeg, yt-dlp, the FilmCraft editor, fonts, and open AI models (including
Whisper, MiniLM, Qwen3, Supertonic 3 and SDXS). Each is licensed by its own authors under
its own license, not under this Agreement. Those licenses are listed in the
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES file distributed with the Software. Nothing in this Agreement limits
the rights those licenses give you over those components.

Some AI model licenses (for example, the OpenRAIL licenses of the Supertonic 3 voice model
and the SDXS image model) include use restrictions. By using those features you agree to
follow those restrictions.

The Software may show links to third-party websites, such as clipping marketplaces.
Licensor does not control or endorse those websites and is not responsible for them.


8. Privacy and internet connections

The Software processes your videos on your own computer. It does not send your videos,
transcripts or clips to Licensor, and it does not collect usage analytics or telemetry.

The Software connects to the internet only to:

  a) check GitHub for updates and download them;
  b) download its Python environment, FFmpeg and other tools during setup;
  c) download AI models from Hugging Face the first time you use each one;
  d) download videos and read public channel information from links you provide; and
  e) open websites you choose, such as YouTube or a clipping marketplace, in its own
     browser window.

Those services have their own terms and privacy policies.


9. Updates

The Software checks for updates and offers to install them. Updates are part of the
Software and are governed by this Agreement, unless an update comes with its own terms,
which then apply instead.


10. Termination

This Agreement applies until it is terminated. It ends automatically if you break any of
its terms. Licensor may also end it, or stop offering the Software, at any time. When it
ends, you must stop using the Software and delete every copy you have. Sections 1, 3, 5,
6, 7, 11, 12 and 13 survive termination. Your Content remains yours.


